module bindings.php.compiler_node_attribute_generated_method_call;

// A template engine that compiles to PHP turns markup the template author
// wrote into generated code, and whatever that code declares runs when the
// compiled template is included. A name the engine's parser stored from
// markup — read back through the documented Node::getAttribute() accessor —
// is author-chosen text, and the one position it may never occupy unquoted
// is a bare identifier in generated code. Twig's macro reference is the
// shape: `_self.('greet')` and `{% import %}` references store the name on
// the node, and compile() emits it raw at a method-call position,
//
//   $compiler->raw(\sprintf('->%s', $this->getAttribute('name')))
//
// so a template naming its macro reference `foo + 1; trigger_error("BAD") //`
// splices PHP into the compiled output — a sandbox escape from inside a
// sandboxed environment. The engine's own safe route is Compiler::repr(),
// which quotes the value; the splice above is not that.
//
// The splice and the attribute read must be one expression, so the clause
// matches the sprintf argument token of the raw-emission call itself. Two
// separate clauses (any `->%s` splice plus any attribute read anywhere in
// the unit) cross-satisfy: measured on this engine's own CallExpression,
// where a reflected-callable splice `sprintf('->%s', $callable[1])` and an
// unrelated error-message sprintf over getAttribute() 255 lines apart
// together satisfied both. The same engine also splices `->%s` formats from
// engine-internal values (a literal-validated local method name, a reflected
// PHP callable); those carry no attribute read inside the splice argument
// and do not match. The validation clause is over call tokens, which are
// AST-derived, so a commented-out preg_match does not count as validation
// and neither does prose naming one. A unit that preg_matches any string is
// quiet even when the spliced name is unvalidated — false-negative
// direction, the same residual the Smarty compile-plugin binding carries.
binding compilerNodeAttributeGeneratedMethodCall {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "module" and node.context.language == "php"
    and containsAny(node.context.callArg, ["sprintf('->%s',$this->getAttribute('", "sprintf(\"->%s\",$this->getAttribute(\""])
    and not containsAny(node.context.call, ["preg_match", "ctype_alnum", "ctype_alpha", "ctype_digit", "ctype_xdigit", "filter_var"])
  emit issue code.IncompleteTemplateValidation at node
}
